'''Qym''' ([[IPA]]: /qɪːm/) is a country in the continent of [[Meran]] on the planet [[Basis]]. It borders [[Afarut]], [[Holaria]], [[Nykal]] and [[Tamodia]] to the west, [[Gosaria]] and [[Imendia]] to the east, and [[Prugundy]] and [[Thyon]] to the south. 

At AREA km² and a population over 162 million inhabitants, Qym is the largest and most populous country in Meran. The capital and largest city is [[Zhol]], and other major urban centers include [[Nagur]], [[Patsalys]], [[Byvichek]] and [[Teurek]]. 

During the [[wikipedia:Iron Age|Iron Age]], the territory of present-day Qym was inhabited by the [[Byrakans]]<!--ANCIENT QYMISH--> before falling under [[Ottelians|Ottelian]] rule in {{abbr|425 BCE|-353 (Earth Year Equivalent)}} following the [[Byrakan Wars]]. The [[Sukats]] settled there in the early 3rd century and founded the [[Sukats Kingdom]] in {{abbr|296 CE|246 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. Their empire collapsed and was partitioned in {{abbr|1100|914 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, and [[Northern Sukatia]] became the [[Duchy of Qym]], subordinate to the [[NEIGHBORING EMPIRE]]. By {{abbr|1453|1207 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, the [[Duchy of Qym]] became the [[Principality of Qym]], with increasing importance in the region. In {{abbr|1918|1593 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, the Kingdom of Qym was established by [[Bacha I of Qym|Bacha I]] and has been a major power in [[Meran]] ever since. In {{abbr|2193|1822 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, the [[Fundamental Law of Qym]] was adopted by King [[Bacha XII of Qym|Bacha XII]], greatly modernizing the country but remaining an [[wikipedia:absolute monarchy|absolute monarchy]] under the rule of the [[House of Zhifol]]. By the end of the 23rd century, Qym had become a leading industrial power and was one of the principal belligerents in the [[Boreal War]] and the subsequent [[Austral War]], winning the former but losing the latter. 

In {{abbr|2334|1939 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, Qym played a key role in the establishment of the [[Basis Forum]]. It is also a member of the [[Meranian Diplomatic League]], the [[International Trade Federation]] and the [[Basis Climatic Organization]], and hosts the headquarters of several international organizations, including the [[Basis Development Bank]], the [[Boreal Cooperation Council]], and the [[Organization of Sukatic Nations]]. Qym is a developed country with one of the largest economies on Basis. It is a global leader in the automotive, aerospace, nuclear and pharmaceutical industries, in addition to making significant contributions to science and technology. Qym is a [[List of countries on Basis with nuclear weapons|nuclear-weapon state]] with the [[List of countries on Basis by number of military and paramilitary personnel|?th-largest standing army by military personnel]] on Basis and the [[List of countries on Basis by military expenditure|?th-largest defense budget]]. It wields considerable political, economic, military, diplomatic, and cultural influence in [[Meran]] and the rest of [[Basis]], making it a [[wikipedia:great power|great power]]. 

==Etymology==
The etymological origin of the name ''Qym'' is uncertain. One plausible explanation is the [[Byrakan language|Byrakan]] cognate ''Qy-im'', meaning "Land of squirrels". 

There is also the claim that ''Qym'' derives from the [[Proto-Sukatic language|Proto-Sukatic]] word ''Khiim'', meaning "WTVR". 

